//www.va.gov/geriatrics/pages/Hospice_Care.asp"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-palliative", "name": "VA palliative care", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/geriatrics/pages/Palliative_Care.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Palliative care addresses symptoms, comfort and care goals for serious illness.", "next_step": "Ask the treating clinician about palliative care options.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/geriatrics/pages/Palliative_Care.asp"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-pension-medicaid-rule", "name": "VA pension during Medicaid-covered nursing home care", "official_url": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-38/section-3.551", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "VA pension payments can be affected by Medicaid-covered nursing home care. The rules depend on the beneficiary\u2019s circumstances.", "next_step": "Ask an accredited representative and the care facility\u2019s benefits staff to review VA pension and Medicaid together before changing benefits.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-02"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-38/section-3.551"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-survivors-pension", "name": "Survivors Pension", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/family-and-caregiver-benefits/survivor-compensation/survivors-pension/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "A potential monthly benefit for qualifying surviving spouses and dependent children of wartime veterans, subject to income, net worth and other requirements.", "next_step": "Ask an accredited representative to screen for Survivors Pension and explain the evidence needed.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/family-and-caregiver-benefits/survivor-compensation/survivors-pension/"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-va-burial", "name": "VA burial allowance and memorial routes", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/burials-memorials/veterans-burial-allowance/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Ask the county office or VA burial program about the correct application.", "next_step": "Ask the county office or VA burial program about the correct application.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-02"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/burials-memorials/veterans-burial-allowance/"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-va-clc", "name": "VA Community Living Centers", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/GERIATRICS/pages/VA_Community_Living_Centers.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "VA-operated Community Living Centers provide nursing home level care for eligible veterans.", "next_step": "Ask the VA care team or social worker about eligibility, assessment and local availability.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/GERIATRICS/pages/VA_Community_Living_Centers.asp"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-va-cnh", "name": "VA Community Nursing Home program", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/GERIATRICS/pages/Community_Nursing_Homes.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "A VA pathway for care in participating community nursing homes, subject to eligibility and available services.", "next_step": "Ask the resident\u2019s VA care team or social worker about community nursing home options.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/GERIATRICS/pages/Community_Nursing_Homes.asp"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-va-health-enrollment", "name": "VA health care enrollment", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/health-care/how-to-apply/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Apply for VA health care or get help understanding the enrollment process.", "next_step": "Call VA enrollment or ask your county veterans office about the application and supporting information.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-222-8387", "phone_label": "VA health care enrollment line", "email": null, "contact_type": "office", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/health-care/how-to-apply/"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-va-pension", "name": "Veterans Pension", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/pension/eligibility/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Monthly pension for qualifying wartime veterans who meet age or disability, income, net worth and service requirements.", "next_step": "Ask an accredited representative to screen for pension and explain how care expenses may affect the application.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/pension/eligibility/"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "r02-whv", "name": "We Honor Veterans public resources", "official_url": "https://www.wehonorveterans.org/about/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Use public veteran-care resources and ask the clinical team about coordinated care.", "next_step": "Use public veteran-care resources and ask the clinical team about coordinated care.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "eligibility": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-02"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.wehonorveterans.org/about/"}, "organization": "National Alliance for Care at Home", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-hisa", "name": "VA Home Improvements and Structural Alterations (HISA)", "official_url": "https://www.rehab.va.gov/PROSTHETICS/psas/HISA2.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["equipment_home_accessibility"], "description": "Medically necessary changes to a veteran\u2019s primary home, including permanent ramps, accessible bathrooms and widened access. Some non-service-connected needs can qualify.", "next_step": "Ask your VA care team for a clinical review and contact your VA medical facility\u2019s Prosthetic and Sensory Aids Service. Confirm your remaining lifetime benefit and obtain the HISA application checklist.", "constraints": ["HISA excludes portable ramps, stair glides, new construction and routine home repairs. VA determines eligibility, medical necessity and the available benefit. Prepare VA Form 10-0103, a VA-written or approved prescription, owner authorization (notarized for renters), an itemized estimate and a before photograph."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "identity": "official_source_reviewed", "contact": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": "web_form_or_locator", "web_route": "https://www.va.gov/find-locations/?facilityType=health"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-sah", "name": "VA Specially Adapted Housing (SAH) grant", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/disability-housing-grants/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["equipment_home_accessibility"], "description": "A housing grant route for veterans with qualifying service-connected disabilities.", "next_step": "Review the qualifying disability and ownership rules with VA or an accredited representative. Apply online through VA or use VA Form 26-4555; ask VA about project planning and approval before construction.", "constraints": ["These grants require specific qualifying service-connected disabilities; a disability rating alone does not establish eligibility. Confirm the current fiscal-year maximum and any benefit already used with VA."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": null, "web_route": null}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-sha", "name": "VA Special Housing Adaptation (SHA) grant", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/disability-housing-grants/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["equipment_home_accessibility"], "description": "A housing adaptation grant route with specific service-connected disability requirements.", "next_step": "Review the qualifying disability and ownership rules with VA or an accredited representative. Apply online through VA or use VA Form 26-4555; ask VA about project planning and approval before construction.", "constraints": ["These grants require specific qualifying service-connected disabilities; a disability rating alone does not establish eligibility. Confirm the current fiscal-year maximum and any benefit already used with VA."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null, "phone_label": null, "email": null, "contact_type": null, "web_route": null}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "nara-discharge-records", "name": "Get a missing DD214 or service record", "official_url": "https://www.archives.gov/veterans/military-service-records", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Request military records that may help document service for a benefits application.", "next_step": "Use the National Archives request instructions or ask the county veterans office for help. Who may request records and any fee depend on the record and request.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "314-801-0800"}, "organization": "National Archives and Records Administration", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-accredited-help", "name": "Find accredited help with a VA claim", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/get-help-from-accredited-representative/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Find and appoint an accredited representative for a benefits claim or decision review. Accredited VSO claims assistance is free.", "next_step": "Use VA\u2019s representative search, then ask the representative if they are available. Attorneys and claims agents may charge fees.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-location-finder", "name": "Find a VA medical facility or benefits office", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/find-locations/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "care_facilities"], "description": "Search for VA locations near the resident and identify where to ask about care or benefits.", "next_step": "Use the official locator with the resident\u2019s city or ZIP code and select the kind of facility needed.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-housing-help", "name": "Veteran housing and homelessness help", "official_url": "https://department.va.gov/homeless/nationalcallcenter/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "A 24-hour VA contact for veterans who are homeless or at risk of losing housing.", "next_step": "Call 877-424-3838, available 24/7, if homeless or at risk of losing housing. Family, care teams and supporters may also call. Ask for local VA and community housing support.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-424-3838"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-tra", "name": "VA Temporary Residence Adaptation (TRA)", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/disability-housing-grants/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["equipment_home_accessibility", "general_navigation"], "description": "Changes to a family member\u2019s home where a qualifying veteran or service member is living temporarily.", "next_step": "Ask VA about TRA if you qualify for SAH or SHA and are temporarily living in a family member\u2019s home.", "constraints": ["TRA requires SAH or SHA eligibility; it is not a general temporary-housing or renter grant."], "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "alz-dementia-support", "name": "Memory loss and dementia: 24/7 support", "official_url": "https://www.alz.org/help-support/i-have-alz/programs-support", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["general_navigation"], "description": "Free, confidential dementia information, caregiver support and referrals to local community resources.", "next_step": "Call the Alzheimer\u2019s Association helpline for care planning, local support groups and caregiver guidance. Seek medical evaluation for new memory concerns.", "constraints": ["The helpline provides support and referrals; it does not replace clinical assessment or emergency services."], "organization": "Alzheimer\u2019s Association", "public_contact": {"phone": "800-272-3900"}, "senior_topic": "memory", "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "american-legion-post-locator", "name": "American Legion: find a local post", "official_url": "https://mylegion.org/PersonifyEbusiness/Find-a-Post", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["general_navigation"], "description": "Official post lookup for community connections and identifying public contacts to share the guide with.", "next_step": "Search the official directory for your town or ZIP code. Confirm the post\u2019s public phone or email and ask who handles community partnerships.", "constraints": ["A local post is not automatically an accredited claims office or a funding provider. Confirm its services, membership or visitor rules, accessibility and current contact details."], "organization": "The American Legion", "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "resource_role": "community_locator", "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "amvets-post-locator", "name": "AMVETS: find a local post", "official_url": "https://www.amvets.org/find-a-post", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["general_navigation"], "description": "Official post lookup for community connections and identifying public contacts to share the guide with.", "next_step": "Search the official directory for your town or ZIP code. Confirm the post\u2019s public phone or email and ask who handles community partnerships.", "constraints": ["A local post is not automatically an accredited claims office or a funding provider. Confirm its services, membership or visitor rules, accessibility and current contact details."], "organization": "AMVETS", "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "resource_role": "community_locator", "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "vfw-post-locator", "name": "VFW: find a local post", "official_url": "https://vfw.org/find-a-post", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["general_navigation"], "description": "Official post lookup for community connections and identifying public contacts to share the guide with.", "next_step": "Search the official directory for your town or ZIP code. Confirm the post\u2019s public phone or email and ask who handles community partnerships.", "constraints": ["A local post is not automatically an accredited claims office or a funding provider. Confirm its services, membership or visitor rules, accessibility and current contact details."], "organization": "Veterans of Foreign Wars", "public_contact": {"phone": null}, "resource_role": "community_locator", "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "crisis-988", "name": "Suicide and emotional crisis support: 988", "official_url": "https://988lifeline.org?oai_link_source=model_response_hotline", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Crisis counseling and referrals for people in suicidal crisis or emotional distress, including veterans and concerned supporters.", "next_step": "Call or text 988 for crisis support. Veterans-specific support is available through the call service. For immediate danger, call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department.", "constraints": ["Crisis support is separate from benefits eligibility and scheduled mental health treatment."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "988"}, "organization": "988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-mental-health", "name": "Veterans: mental health care and suicide prevention", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/health-care/health-needs-conditions/mental-health/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "VA mental health care, suicide-prevention guidance, counseling and routes to VA medical centers and Vet Centers. Some services are available without VA enrollment.", "next_step": "Use the VA page to connect with care. Existing patients can ask their primary care provider; others can contact a VA medical center or Vet Center. For urgent emotional distress, use 988 instead of waiting for an appointment.", "constraints": ["Confirm which services fit the person\u2019s eligibility and needs. Scheduled care is not a substitute for immediate crisis help."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-ssvf", "name": "Housing stability: Supportive Services for Veteran Families (SSVF)", "official_url": "https://department.va.gov/homeless/supportive-services-for-veteran-families/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Housing stability services through community organizations for low-income veteran families experiencing homelessness or imminent housing loss.", "next_step": "Use the SSVF Providers link on the VA page to find an awarded organization. Ask about county coverage, prevention or rapid rehousing, eligibility and current assistance.", "constraints": ["Provider service areas, funding and eligibility vary. An award or referral does not guarantee financial assistance."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {}, "organization": "VA-funded community SSVF providers", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-hud-vash", "name": "HUD-VASH: housing vouchers and VA support", "official_url": "https://department.va.gov/homeless/hud-vash/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Housing voucher assistance paired with VA case management for veterans experiencing homelessness who need ongoing support.", "next_step": "Call VA homelessness routing at 877-424-3838 and ask whether HUD-VASH screening is appropriate. Ask about local assessment, vouchers and housing availability.", "constraints": ["Screening, program criteria, voucher availability and qualifying housing requirements apply; immediate housing is not guaranteed."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-424-3838"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs / HUD", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-crrc", "name": "VA Community Resource and Referral Centers", "official_url": "https://department.va.gov/homeless/hchv/community-resource-and-referral-centers/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Find walk-in community resource centers connecting homeless and at-risk veterans with VA and non-VA services.", "next_step": "Use the official center directory and confirm the nearest location, hours and intake. If no nearby center is listed, call VA homelessness routing at 877-424-3838.", "constraints": ["Centers are not present in every county. Confirm local access and resources; a listing does not guarantee a shelter bed."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-10-08"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-424-3838"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-disability-compensation", "name": "VA disability compensation", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/disability/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Compensation for veterans with an illness or injury connected to their military service, including conditions VA presumes are service-connected.", "next_step": "A county veterans office or another accredited representative can help you file. You can also file online, by mail or in person. For questions, call the VA benefits hotline, Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 9 p.m. ET.", "constraints": ["VA decides eligibility and ratings. This guide does not prepare or file claims."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "800-827-1000"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-supplemental-claims", "name": "Disagree with a VA decision: Supplemental Claims", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/decision-reviews/supplemental-claim/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "A way to ask VA to look again at a decided claim when you have new and relevant evidence, or when the law has changed.", "next_step": "Ask an accredited representative whether this review fits your decision. A Supplemental Claim can be filed online for disability compensation, or by mail or in person for other benefits.", "constraints": ["This is one of VA's decision review options. An accredited representative can explain the choices."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-pact-act", "name": "Toxic exposure and the PACT Act", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/resources/the-pact-act-and-your-va-benefits/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "The PACT Act expands VA health care and benefits for veterans exposed to burn pits, Agent Orange and other toxic substances, including veterans of the Vietnam, Gulf War and post-9/11 eras.", "next_step": "Ask for a toxic exposure screening at your next VA health care appointment, or contact your local VA health facility and ask for the toxic exposure screening navigator. For questions, call VA at 800-698-2411.", "constraints": ["The screening is for veterans enrolled in VA health care. VA decides eligibility for care and benefits."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "800-698-2411"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-women-veterans-call-center", "name": "Women Veterans Call Center", "official_url": "https://www.womenshealth.va.gov/wvcc.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "A free, confidential VA line that helps women veterans find VA services and resources. A friend, relative or caregiver may call for her.", "next_step": "Call or text 855-829-6636, Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 10 p.m. ET, and Saturday, 8 a.m. to 6:30 p.m. ET, or use the online chat on the VA page.", "constraints": ["Closed on federal holidays. In a crisis, call 988 and press 1."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "855-829-6636"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-vet-centers", "name": "Vet Centers: counseling in your community", "official_url": "https://www.vetcenter.va.gov/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Community counseling centers that offer individual, group, marriage and family counseling at no cost to eligible veterans, service members (including National Guard and Reserve) and their families.", "next_step": "Call the Vet Center Call Center at 877-927-8387, at any hour, to talk with someone or to be connected with the nearest Vet Center.", "constraints": ["Eligibility depends on the kind of service or experience, such as service in a combat theater or military sexual trauma. Ask the Vet Center."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-927-8387"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-vet-center-mst", "name": "Counseling after military sexual trauma", "official_url": "https://www.vetcenter.va.gov/Military_Sexual_Trauma.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Counseling at Vet Centers for any veteran or service member, including National Guard and Reserve members, who experienced military sexual trauma, whenever they served.", "next_step": "Call the Vet Center Call Center at 877-927-8387 and ask about military sexual trauma counseling. In a crisis, call 988 and press 1.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-927-8387"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-gi-bill", "name": "GI Bill and VA education benefits", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/education/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Help paying for college, job training and career counseling for veterans, service members and qualified family members.", "next_step": "Check eligibility and apply on VA's education page, or call the GI Bill hotline, Monday through Friday, 7 a.m. to 6 p.m. Central. A school's VA certifying official can also help you apply.", "constraints": ["Benefits depend on your service and the program you choose. VA decides eligibility."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "888-442-4551"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-vre", "name": "Veteran Readiness and Employment (Chapter 31)", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/careers-employment/vocational-rehabilitation/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "employment_transition"], "description": "Job training, help finding or returning to work, self-employment support and independent living services for veterans and service members whose service-connected disability limits their ability to work.", "next_step": "Apply online, by mail or at a VA regional office. If you are eligible, VA invites you to an orientation session.", "constraints": ["For veterans, VA's eligibility page asks for a service-connected disability rating of at least 10% and a discharge that is not dishonorable."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "dol-american-job-centers", "name": "Job help at American Job Centers", "official_url": "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/eta/jobs-for-veterans-act", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "employment_transition"], "description": "Employment and training services through a national network of more than 2,400 American Job Centers. Veterans and eligible spouses receive priority of service in U.S. Department of Labor job training programs.", "next_step": "Find the nearest American Job Center at careeronestop.org or call 877-872-5627. Tell the staff you are a veteran or an eligible spouse so priority of service applies.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-872-5627"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Labor", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-home-loans", "name": "VA home loans", "official_url": "https://benefits.va.gov/homeloans/index.asp", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "VA-backed home loans for veterans, service members and eligible surviving spouses.", "next_step": "Start by getting a Certificate of Eligibility, online or through your lender. To speak with a VA loan technician, call 877-827-3702.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "877-827-3702"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-veteran-id-cards", "name": "Veteran ID cards", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/records/get-veteran-id-cards/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Ways to show veteran status: the digital Veteran ID Card, the Veteran Health Identification Card used at VA appointments, a Department of Defense ID, or a veteran designation on a state driver's license or ID.", "next_step": "Choose the card that fits you on VA's page and apply online. Have your discharge papers ready for the Veteran ID Card.", "constraints": ["The Veteran ID Card is for veterans with an honorable or general discharge. The health ID card requires enrollment in VA health care."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-discharge-upgrade", "name": "Discharge upgrade or correction", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/resources/request-a-discharge-upgrade-or-correction/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "general_navigation"], "description": "Step-by-step instructions for asking a military board to upgrade or correct a discharge. If the discharge is upgraded, the veteran becomes eligible for the VA benefits earned during that period of service.", "next_step": "Answer the questions on VA's page to get the forms and the mailing address for your situation, or ask a veterans service organization to help. For questions, call 800-827-1000, Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 9 p.m. ET.", "constraints": ["You apply by mail or with the help of a veterans service organization."], "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "800-827-1000"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "va-solid-start", "name": "VA Solid Start: your first year out", "official_url": "https://www.va.gov/service-member-benefits/solid-start/", "service_area": ["National"], "needs_supported": ["veteran_services", "employment_transition"], "description": "VA representatives contact newly separated service members three times during the first year after active duty to explain benefits such as health care, housing assistance and education.", "next_step": "Keep your contact information with VA up to date and take the call. To reach Solid Start, call 800-827-0611, Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 9 p.m. ET.", "constraints": null, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-17"}, "public_contact": {"phone": "800-827-0611"}, "organization": "U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs", "state": "shared"}, {"program_id": "la-claims", "name": "Louisiana veterans: parish veterans service offices for claims help", "official_url": "https://vetaffairs.la.gov/locations", "organization": "Louisiana Department of Veterans Affairs", "service_area": ["statewide"], "state": "LA", "needs_supported": ["general_navigation", "benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Free help with VA claims, appeals, pension and survivor benefits from Louisiana Department of Veterans Affairs staff. Every parish is served by a department office.", "next_step": "Choose your parish for its office and open days, or call the department at 225-219-5000 (Monday\u2013Friday 8:00 a.m.\u20134:00 p.m.).", "constraints": ["Many parish offices are open only one to three days a week; check the days and call before you go."], "public_contact": {"phone": "225-219-5000", "phone_label": "Louisiana Department of Veterans Affairs (225-219-5000)"}, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-16"}, "evidence": {"review_method": "full_official_page_text", "direct_agency_confirmation": false, "phone_source_url": "https://vetaffairs.la.gov/locations/headquarters"}, "source_evidence": [{"url": "https://vetaffairs.la.gov/locations", "title": "Louisiana Department of Veterans Affairs: Locations", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Lists the parish veterans service offices and itinerant points; links to each office page."}, {"url": "https://vetaffairs.la.gov/locations/headquarters", "title": "Louisiana Department of Veterans Affairs: Headquarters", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Address, phone 225-219-5000 and hours; read in full."}]}, {"program_id": "la-adrc", "name": "Louisiana Answers: aging and disability information line", "official_url": "https://goea.la.gov/agency-directory/aging-and-disability-resource-centers", "organization": "Governor\u2019s Office of Elderly Affairs, Aging and Disability Resource Centers", "service_area": ["statewide"], "state": "LA", "needs_supported": ["general_navigation", "help_at_home", "equipment_home_accessibility"], "description": "Louisiana\u2019s Aging and Disability Resource Centers help older adults and adults with disabilities find long-term care options, prescription assistance and local services. The statewide information, referral and assistance line connects you to the center for your parish. Military service is not required.", "next_step": "Call 877-340-9100, or choose a parish above for its Area Agency on Aging.", "constraints": ["Each program has its own eligibility and waitlist.", "Give your parish so the call reaches the right center."], "public_contact": {"phone": "877-340-9100", "phone_label": "Louisiana Answers (877-340-9100)"}, "verification": {"record_status": "official_search_extract_only", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-16"}, "evidence": {"review_method": "official_search_excerpt", "direct_agency_confirmation": false, "phone_source_url": "https://laddc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/DD-Council-Report-April-2026.pdf"}, "source_evidence": [{"url": "https://laddc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/DD-Council-Report-April-2026.pdf", "title": "Governor\u2019s Office of Elderly Affairs report to the Louisiana Developmental Disabilities Council (April 2026)", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Nine Aging and Disability Resource Centers, housed in an Area Agency on Aging or council on aging; statewide information, referral and assistance line 877-340-9100; search excerpt."}, {"url": "https://goea.la.gov/agency-directory/aging-and-disability-resource-centers", "title": "Governor\u2019s Office of Elderly Affairs: Aging and Disability Resource Centers directory", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Centers and the parishes each serves; search excerpt."}]}, {"program_id": "la-ship", "name": "Medicare counseling (SHIIP) for Louisiana", "official_url": "https://ldi.la.gov/consumers/senior-health-shiip", "organization": "Louisiana Department of Insurance, Senior Health Insurance Information Program (SHIIP)", "service_area": ["statewide"], "state": "LA", "needs_supported": ["benefits_and_funding"], "description": "Free, confidential Medicare counseling from the Department of Insurance\u2019s Senior Health Insurance Information Program and its partner counselors around the state: plan choices, enrollment, costs and help paying for Medicare. The department also calls it LaSHIP.", "next_step": "Call 800-259-5300 and ask for a SHIIP counselor, or use the department\u2019s page to find help near you. For Medicare itself, call 800-MEDICARE (800-633-4227).", "constraints": ["Have your Medicare card and drug list ready."], "public_contact": {"phone": "800-259-5300", "phone_label": "Louisiana Department of Insurance, SHIIP (800-259-5300)"}, "verification": {"record_status": "official_search_extract_only", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-16"}, "evidence": {"review_method": "official_search_excerpt", "direct_agency_confirmation": false, "phone_source_url": "https://www.ldi.la.gov/docs/default-source/documents/shiip/guide-to-navigating-medicare.pdf"}, "source_evidence": [{"url": "https://ldi.la.gov/consumers/senior-health-shiip", "title": "Louisiana Department of Insurance: Senior Health Insurance Information Program", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Program description and a link to find help near you; read in full. The page prints no phone number."}, {"url": "https://www.ldi.la.gov/docs/default-source/documents/shiip/guide-to-navigating-medicare.pdf", "title": "Louisiana Department of Insurance: Guide to Navigating Medicare", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Phone 1-800-259-5300 and LDI.LA.GOV/LaSHIP; search excerpt."}, {"url": "https://www.cms.gov/about-cms/contact/directory/senior-health-insurance-information-program-shiip/1562086", "title": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services: SHIIP contact directory entry", "reviewed_on": "2026-11-16", "scope": "Louisiana SHIIP toll-free (800) 259-5300; search excerpt."}]}, {"program_id": "la-ombudsman", "name": "Louisiana Long-Term Care Ombudsman and elder abuse reporting", "official_url": "https://goea.louisiana.gov/services/louisiana-ombudsman-program", "organization": "Governor\u2019s Office of Elderly Affairs, Long-Term Care Ombudsman Program", "service_area": ["statewide"], "state": "LA", "needs_supported": ["resident_rights", "general_navigation"], "description": "Independent advocacy for residents of nursing homes and assisted living, through seven regional programs and the state office.", "next_step": "Call the state ombudsman office at 866-632-0922, or choose a parish above for its regional ombudsman. To report abuse, neglect or exploitation of someone 60 or older, call Elderly Protective Services at 833-577-6532 (after hours: 844-945-2377). For adults 18 to 59, call Adult Protective Services at 800-898-4910. In an emergency, call 911.", "constraints": ["The ombudsman acts with the resident\u2019s permission and is not a licensing agency."], "public_contact": {"phone": "866-632-0922", "phone_label": "Louisiana State Long-Term Care Ombudsman (866-632-0922)"}, "verification": {"record_status": "official_source_reviewed", "last_reviewed_on": "2026-11-16"}, "evidence": {"review_method": "full_official_pdf", "direct_agency_confirmation": false, "phone_source_url": "ht